## Why This Is Asked
Understanding end-to-end streaming ingestion, privacy handling, and basic rollback in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming
- Dataflow DoFn masking
- BigQuery per-tenant datasets
- Data Catalog data contracts and lineage
- Quarantine path and 24h rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow DoFn: mask PII before write
class MaskPIIFn {
  process(element) {
    // element is a JSON object
    if (element.email) element.email = maskEmail(element.email);
    if (element.phone) element.phone = maskPhone(element.phone);
    return element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this pipeline for schema drift and masking correctness?
- How would you alert on quarantine volume spikes and auto-remediate?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical handling of evolving data in a streaming pipeline, balancing query stability with schema growth.

## Key Concepts
- Schema evolution in BigQuery
- Semi-structured data (JSON)
- Dataflow transforms for parsing
- Backward compatibility
- Metadata and cataloging

## Code Example
```javascript
function parseEvent(json) {
  const data = JSON.parse(json);
  const known = {
    userId: data.user_id || null,
    eventTime: data.event_time || null,
    country: data.country || null
  };
  const extraKeys = Object.keys(data).filter(k => !(k in known));
  const extra = JSON.stringify(extraKeys.reduce((acc, k) => { acc[k] = data[k]; return acc; }, {}));
  return { ...known, extra_json: extra };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
